.TITLE "scutil"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Manages and queries system configuration parameters on macOS. This command-line
utility allows users to inspect and modify network settings, hostname, DNS
configuration, and other system-level preferences managed by the `SystemConfiguration`
framework. It is a powerful tool for network diagnostics and configuration.

.DIV "ALIAS"
**sysconfig**

.DIV "TLDR"
**scutil --get __HostName__**
Gets the current system hostname.
> __HostName__: The SystemConfiguration key to retrieve.

**scutil --set __HostName__ __MyMacbook__**
Sets the system hostname to __MyMacbook__.
> __HostName__: The SystemConfiguration key to set. | __MyMacbook__: The new value for the hostname.

**scutil --dns**
Displays the current DNS configuration, including resolver settings.
> 

**scutil --get __ComputerName__**
Gets the computer name displayed in Finder and System Settings.
> __ComputerName__: The SystemConfiguration key to retrieve.

**scutil --set __LocalHostName__ __mymacbook__**
Sets the local hostname for Bonjour/mDNS.
> __LocalHostName__: The SystemConfiguration key to set. | __mymacbook__: The new value for the local hostname.

.DIV "SUMMARY"
`scutil` provides granular control over network and system identification settings.
Changes made with `scutil --set` are typically persistent across reboots.
Misconfigurations can affect network connectivity, so exercise caution.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**mac:networksetup**

